Close, but not quite correct.  In England I could, and many do, sue the
distributor and vendor as well as the newspaper.  No-one sues the reporter,
as the newspaper is clearly responsible for what is printed.  Similarly
the universities who give their users computer accounts and access to the 
usenet are clearly responsible for what goes out on it.

It may be that the 
users who post such libels are obliged to indemnify the universities - that
is between them and their universities, and is not my concern.  It is not
equivalent to suing the local neighbourhood newsstand, as you suggest,
